  "name": null,
  "problem": "Catherine used $9\\,\\frac{2}{7}$ liters of distilled water out of $10\\,\\frac{3}{4}$ liters of distilled water available. What is the volume of the remaining distilled water? Express your answer as a mixed number.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The volume of distilled water remaining equals$\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,$liters.",
  "worked_solution": "Caterine had $(10\\,\\frac{3}{4}-9\\,\\frac{2}{7})$ liters of distilled water left over.\n\nWriting $10\\,\\frac{3}{4}$ as an improper fraction, we have\n\n$$\n10\\,\\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{10\\times 4+3}{4}=\\frac{43}{4}.\n$$\n\nWriting $9\\,\\frac{2}{7}$ as an improper fraction, we have\n\n$$\n9\\,\\frac{2}{7}=\\frac{9\\times 7+2}{7}=\\frac{65}{7}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our problem now is to work out the following:\n\n$$\n\\frac{43}{4}-\\frac{65}{7}\n$$\n\nTo subtract two fractions with unlike denominators, we need to express each fraction as an equivalent fraction with a common denominator.\n\nIn this question, we can make a common denominator of $28.$\n\nTo put $\\frac{43}{4}$ over a denominator of $28,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator by $7:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{43}{4}=\\frac{43\\times 7}{4\\times 7}=\\frac{301}{28}\n$$\n\nTo put $\\frac{65}{7}$ over a denominator of $28,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{65}{7}=\\frac{65\\times 4}{7\\times 4}=\\frac{260}{28}\n$$\n\nWe can now subtract the fractions. We keep the denominator the same, and we subtract the numerators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{301}{28}-\\frac{260}{28}=\\frac{41}{28}\n$$\n\nFinally, we convert back to a mixed number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{41}{28}=1\\,\\text{R}\\,13=1\\,\\frac{13}{28}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of distilled water remaining equals $1\\,\\frac{13}{28}$ liters.",
